course: dictionary
lesson: 4119
title: Glance: a quick look
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To glance is to look at something very quickly and then look away. A glance is a quick look. «Leo glanced at the test answers on her desk, then owned up to the teacher.» She looked for only a moment, and glanced tells you it was quick, not a long stare.
explain: Glance can also mean hitting something at an angle and bouncing off to the side. Drivers and cyclists glance in mirrors and over their shoulders, a quick check that keeps them safe. «At a glance» means you understand something straight away, like a chart in maths.
explain: Look at the words around glance to work out its meaning. «Keeley smiles, and keeps glancing at the phone, wishing her mum would call.» Keeps glancing shows she looks at the phone again and again, quickly, because she is waiting for a call.
fact: Glance is a verb (glance, glances, glanced, glancing) and a noun (a glance, glances).
fact: «Glanced» means looked at something quickly and then looked away.
fact: «The hour has come!» asks the Rat, «glancing at the clock», which means he looks at it quickly.
fact: «Exchange glances» means two people look at each other to share a feeling without words.
fact: «At first glance» means when you first see something, before you look closely.
exercise: «Leo glanced at the test answers on her desk, then owned up.» What does glanced mean here? | *Stared at them for an hour | Wrote the answers down carefully | Hid them under a book | Looked at very quickly, then looked away
exercise: «Keeley keeps glancing at the phone, wishing her mum would call.» Why does Keeley keep glancing? | *She is waiting and hoping for a call | She is reading a book | She is writing a story | She is bored and wants to sleep
exercise: Which phrase means you can see or understand something straight away? | at the end of the day | in a rush | once upon a time | *at a glance
test: Drivers glance in their mirrors before they change lanes. What does glance mean here? | Stop the car | Close the eyes | *Look quickly | Shout loudly
test: In «She gave him a glance across the room», what kind of word is glance? | Adjective | Verb | Adverb | *Noun
exam: Which sentence uses glance to mean hit something at an angle and bounce away? | *The ball glanced off the goalpost and rolled away | The children glance at the sky | He glanced up from his book | She glanced around the room
